  "interpretation": [
    "Transporter predicts pick/place XY; RGB-D geometry supplies grasp centre refinement, yaw, heights and a feasible-pick mask. It is not fully learned motor control.",
    "Policy receives RGB-D only. Oracle and scoring use privileged simulator state.",
    "All requested test scenes, including runtime errors, count in the denominator. Errors receive zero verified stable objects because the final hold could not be verified.",
    "Success requires all three objects to pass the two-second final hold, within six actions and the between-action 180-second budget.",
    "Episode time is local simulation wall time excluding model loading, not real-robot cycle time.",
    "The collapse counter only detects decreases between completed actions; it does not prove no physical falls occurred.",
    "Ten scenes from known shape families are preliminary evidence, not an unseen-shape or arbitrary-clutter benchmark.",
    "Raw datasets, checkpoints, action traces and screenshots remain local and Git-ignored. This report preserves compact results and artifact identifiers."
  ]
